# esp-hosted-mcu#243 — serial capture from the device the fault was found on.
#
# ESP32-P4 (Elecrow CrowPanel Advance 7") + ESP32-C6. esp_hosted 2.12.13 on BOTH sides.
# SDIO 1-bit @ 10 MHz, STREAMING RX mode, CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_MEMPOOL_PREFER_SPIRAM off
# (its default). CONFIG_ESP_HOSTED_PKT_STATS=y at 2 s, log ceiling raised to INFO so the
# driver's own warning is compiled in — a default ERROR-only build hides it entirely.
#
# Traffic is ordinary product use: browsing a music service over TLS (15-29 KB responses)
# and fetching cover art. No synthetic load.
#
# Four stalls in ~13 minutes, one mechanism each time. Extracted verbatim from a 7,221-line
# capture (09:00-12:39); the full log is available on request.
# Local wall-clock timestamps are prepended by the capture tool; the (NNNN) values are the
# device's own ms.

====================================================================================================
A. BOOT OF THE DIAGNOSTIC BUILD — transport config and versions
# hostedGetHostVersion() reports 2.12.11 only because the Arduino core compiles against the
# platform package's stale prebuilt headers; the LINKED driver is 2.12.13, as the slave line
# and the fix-only log strings in the ELF confirm.
