B1. STALL 1 OF 4 — allocation of 18432 B failed
# `s2h{in[N] out[N]}` FREEZES at the first stats line after the warning and never moves
# again; `h2s ... out(ok[N])` keeps counting, so host->co-processor is unaffected.
# The warning appears EXACTLY ONCE — the 2.12.12 retry (pending=true) never runs, because
# the first pass already cleared NEW_PACKET and the retry pass returns at that gate.
# `internal: free X l-free Y` is 8BIT|INTERNAL, NOT the DMA-capable pool that ran out:
# in B2-B4 the largest general block (31,732 B) EXCEEDS the failing request.
